{
  "track": "es",
  "level": "B1",
  "unit": 3,
  "title": "Right now",
  "description": "Say what is happening at this moment.",
  "explanation": {
    "summary": "The present progressive is for something that is happening now, or that is going on around you. It is estar plus a gerund, and the gerund is made by changing the ending of the infinitive.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Making the gerund",
        "body": "An -ar verb drops the ar and adds ando: hablar becomes hablando. An -er or -ir verb drops the er or ir and adds iendo: comer becomes comiendo, vivir becomes viviendo. Ver becomes viendo, and the stem-changing verbs lose their change: dormir becomes durmiendo.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "Estoy leyendo un libro.",
            "en": "I am reading a book."
          },
          {
            "es": "Estamos comiendo.",
            "en": "We are eating."
          },
          {
            "es": "El niño está durmiendo.",
            "en": "The child is sleeping."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "When to use it",
        "body": "The progressive says what is in progress: ahora estoy trabajando. It also covers the near future, because Spanish has no other way to say what you are about to do: estoy yendo, I am going. And it can be used for a routine that is happening now, like esta semana estoy viajando.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "Ahora estoy trabajando.",
            "en": "Right now I am working."
          },
          {
            "es": "Estoy yendo al mercado.",
            "en": "I am going to the market."
          },
          {
            "es": "Esta semana estoy de vacaciones.",
            "en": "This week I am on holiday."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "With the word for right now",
        "body": "The word ahora goes at the start or the end, and either is fine. But the verb comes before it when it is at the end: estoy trabajando ahora. And Spanish often adds the gerund with estar for something that is going on around you: está lloviendo, it is raining.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "Ahora está lloviendo.",
            "en": "Now it is raining."
          },
          {
            "es": "Está nevando.",
            "en": "It is snowing."
          },
          {
            "es": "Estoy trabajando ahora.",
            "en": "I am working now."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
